-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/f16786fa-e5c6-4e31-8e04-37e4475055d6
-- title:
--   A faithfully flat map identifying local rings between w-local rings, out of a ring with extremally disconnected $\pi_0$, has a retraction
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a w-local ring such that the space $\pi_0(\operatorname{Spec} R)$ of connected components of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ is extremally disconnected, and let $I \subseteq R$ be an ideal whose zero locus $V(I)$ is exactly the set of closed points of $\operatorname{Spec} R$. Let $S$ be an $R$-algebra such that:
--
--   1. $S$ is faithfully flat over $R$;
--   2. $R \to S$ identifies local rings (it is bijective on stalks: $R_{\mathfrak q \cap R} \to S_{\mathfrak q}$ is an isomorphism for every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $S$);
--   3. $S$ is w-local;
--   4. $V(IS)$ is exactly the set of closed points of $\operatorname{Spec} S$.
--
--   Then $R \to S$ has a retraction: there is a ring homomorphism $r : S \to R$ with
--   $$r \circ \varphi = \mathrm{id}_R,$$
--   where $\varphi : R \to S$ is the structure map.
--
--   This is the key step in the characterisation of w-contractible rings (the second part of the proof of (3) $\Rightarrow$ (1) in Stacks, Tag 09AZ).
--
--   **Formalization Note** Both rings are in `Type u`. W-locality is `IsWLocalRing`, extremal disconnectedness is `ExtremallyDisconnected (ConnectedComponents (PrimeSpectrum R))`, faithful flatness is `Module.FaithfullyFlat R S`, and identifying local rings is the class `Algebra.BijectiveOnStalks R S`. The closed-point conditions are `zeroLocus I = closedPoints (PrimeSpectrum R)` and the same for `I.map (algebraMap R S)`. The retraction is a bare ring homomorphism `S →+* R` with `f.comp (algebraMap R S) = RingHom.id R`. The theorem is `exists_retraction_of_bijectiveOnStalks`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014); cited in the code: Stacks Project, Tag 09AZ. Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Algebra/WContractible.lean, lines 644-685 (`exists_retraction_of_bijectiveOnStalks`).

